<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-04T20:19:08+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 04 Nov 2026 20:19:08 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[UN report finds huge gap in adaptation finance ahead of COP31]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/un-report-finds-huge-gap-in-adaptation-finance-ahead-of-cop31/articleshow/135542542.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135542542.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Developing nations require approximately $305 billion annually by 2035 for climate change adaptation efforts. Rich countries' collective pledge could only reach $85-120 billion each year by 2035. While current financial contributions are around $28.2-31.7 billion, this is still inadequate. UN Environment Programme emphasizes the urgent need for increased adaptation financing and overcoming institutional barriers. Action on climate adaptation is essential to mitigate worsening impacts from extreme weather events.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/un-report-finds-huge-gap-in-adaptation-finance-ahead-of-cop31/articleshow/135542542.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/un-report-finds-huge-gap-in-adaptation-finance-ahead-of-cop31/articleshow/135542542.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T20:09:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vishwa Mohan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135542678,imgsize-136518.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[CBI successfully extradites sexual assault accused from UAE after Interpol Red Notice]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbi-successfully-extradites-sexual-assault-accused-from-uae-after-interpol-red-notice/articleshow/135541296.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135541296.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbi-successfully-extradites-sexual-assault-accused-from-uae-after-interpol-red-notice/articleshow/135541296.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cbi-successfully-extradites-sexual-assault-accused-from-uae-after-interpol-red-notice/articleshow/135541296.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T19:41:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135541970,imgsize-150883.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Normalise, recognise and formalise': Nadda accuses Congress of opposing SIR to legitimise outsiders, destabilise country]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/normalise-recognise-and-formalise-nadda-accuses-congress-of-opposing-sir-to-legitimise-outsiders-destabilise-country/articleshow/135541462.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135541462.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Union health minister JP Nadda accused the Congress party of opposing the Special Intensive Revision of voter lists. He alleged that their actions are aimed at protecting outsiders who support their political ambitions. Nadda criticized the Congress for undermining the credibility of the Election Commission when faced with electoral losses. He noted that the current electoral process includes Booth Level Officers facilitating voter registration door-to-door.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/normalise-recognise-and-formalise-nadda-accuses-congress-of-opposing-sir-to-legitimise-outsiders-destabilise-country/articleshow/135541462.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/normalise-recognise-and-formalise-nadda-accuses-congress-of-opposing-sir-to-legitimise-outsiders-destabilise-country/articleshow/135541462.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T19:36:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135541767,imgsize-81806.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[SC rejects woman's plea to terminate six-month pregnancy over marital discord]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-rejects-womans-plea-to-terminate-six-month-pregnancy-over-marital-discord/articleshow/135540949.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135540949.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-rejects-womans-plea-to-terminate-six-month-pregnancy-over-marital-discord/articleshow/135540949.cms]]></link><guid><